{"shortDescription":"The Australian dollar steadied around $0.71, holding its recent decline near a four-week low as a firmer US dollar and higher Treasury yields weighed on the currency ahead of the Federal Reserve’s policy decision.The greenback strengthened as markets widely expected the Fed to raise interest rates…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Australian dollar steadied around $0.71, holding its recent decline near a four-week low as a firmer US dollar and higher Treasury yields weighed on the currency ahead of the Federal Reserve’s policy decision."]},{"type":"p","children":["The greenback strengthened as markets widely expected the Fed to raise interest rates by 25 basis points, its first increase in around three years, while the US 10-year Treasury yield climbed above 5%, its highest level since 2007, as surging oil prices and persistent inflation concerns reinforced expectations for tighter policy."]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices held near a four-month peak above $105 a barrel after fresh Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia and the postponement of Gulf-Iran talks."]},{"type":"p","children":["Domestically, the Reserve Bank of Australia’s hawkish stance continues to provide some support, with markets pricing an 85% probability of a rate increase to 4.60% at its September 29 meeting."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors now await comments from Governor Bullock, which is scheduled to appear before Parliament on Friday."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:584033:0","title":"Australian Dollar Under Pressure Ahead of Fed Decision","published":1789521224,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/australia/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:AUDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/AU","logo":{"style":"p